  "estimator": "threshold = the gap at which the pair-averaged preference for the closer option exceeds one half for at least accuracy_level of pairs, interpolated linearly in log gap between ladder points; infinity if never reached",
  "side": "both",
  "probe_2026-09-08_two_sided": "VACUOUS: accuracy 0.62 to 0.76 at every gap including 10, threshold infinite; the judge picked the larger number in every straddling pair of a six-case diagnostic, and the instrument read space-prefixed letter tokens whose logits sat 25 to 30 below the bare letters the chat template elicits. Both corrected before any pilot.",
  "judge_kind": "scorer",
  "scorer_prompt_template": "Target: {target}\nValue: {value}\nHow far is the value from the target? Answer with a single number and nothing else.",
  "max_new_tokens": 12,
  "probe_2026-09-08_one_sided_chooser": "NOT VACUOUS but floor 7.5: one-sided pairs, bare-letter reading; accuracy 0.99 at gap 10, 0.77 at 5, 0.43 to 0.63 from 0.01 to 2, threshold 7.5, above the 0.3 the anti-vacuity rule allows, because the chooser's first-position preference leaves the two-order average at one half until the gap is large. A pairwise chooser is the wrong instrument for a threshold; replaced by the scorer before any pilot.",
  "report_token_budgets": [
   1,
